nodes.body:
🔵 Minor **[PR Pundit]**

The new tests miss several paths:
- specforge_overrides['model.draft_model_config'] and its precedence over the Hydra file;
- CAPTURE_LAYER_IDS env precedence over the recipe draft;
- the TARGET_MODEL vs recipe target precedence chain;
- the SKIP_TOKENIZER_INIT env var, string values and invalid booleans;
- the missing or malformed draft JSON fallback.
They call online_settings(params) without env=, so an ambient CAPTURE_LAYER_IDS or TARGET_MODEL flips the results. The 'relative to root' test does not control cwd and passes only because cwd lacks the file, so it does not assert root-over-cwd precedence. The tests write into the shared specforge_checkout fixture directory. One test mixes three unrelated assertions under a layer-ids name. The whole TestOnlineLaunch class is skipped outside the overlay.

**Evidence (verified by running it):** weaver-pytest on the specforge test file: 109 skipped ('requires SpecForge overlay image'); the new functions ran fine when called directly on CPU.

files.patch:
@@ -56,6 +56,7 @@ modules:
         mooncake_protocol: ${MOONCAKE_PROTOCOL:tcp}
         mooncake_lease_ttl_ms: ${MOONCAKE_LEASE_TTL_MS:500}
         target_model_path: ${TARGET_MODEL:Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B}
+        # skip_tokenizer_init: true  # or SKIP_TOKENIZER_INIT; false inits the tokenizer

       specforge_overrides:
         training.max_steps: ${MAX_STEPS:20}

